Implement shapes for a 3D scene and the world they live in.

Steps:
- [x] bidimensional vector:
  - [x] implement a type `Vec2D{T}` representing a 2D vector,
        it will be used as a vector on the coordinate system bound to the surface of the shape;
- [x] Shapes:
  - [x] implement an abstract type `Shape`;
  - [x] implement a concrete type `Sphere`,
        it represents a unit sphere and stores the `Transformation` that turns it into its final position and form;
  - [x] implement tests for all of the above;
  - [ ] (optional) implement other shapes;
- [x] record intersections:
  - [x] implement a struct `HitRecord`,
        it must contains the fields: 
        - `world_point`: 3D point of the intersection (`Point`);
        - `normal`: normal to the shape surface at the intersection (`Normal`);
        - `surface_point`: surface coordinates (u,v) of intersection (`Vec2D`);
        - `t`: ray parameter of intersection (`Real`);
        - `ray`: ray part of the intersection (`Ray`).
  - [x] implement `≈` for `HitRecord`.
  - [x] implement function `ray_intersection(::Shape, ::Ray)` for each subtype of `Shape`,
        it must return the `HitRecord` between a shape and a ray
  - [x] implement tests for all of the above;
- [x] world:
  - [x] implement alias `World` for `Vector{Shape}`;
  - [x] implement tests for `World`.

